          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>[EXAM TIP] </strong>Damodar river was called \"Sorrow of Bengal\" due to frequent floods. The Damodar Valley Corporation (DVC) was set up to control floods — it is India's first multipurpose river valley project.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Teesta River originates from Pauhunri Glacier in Sikkim and is often referred to as the 'Lifeline of North Bengal'.",
        "Damodar River was historically known as the 'Sorrow of Bengal' prior to the dam projects under the Damodar Valley Corporation (DVC).",
        "The Rarh region is a distinct physiographic zone situated between the Chota Nagpur Plateau and the Ganges Delta, dominated by red laterite soil.",
        "East Kolkata Wetlands was declared a Ramsar site in 2002 for its unique natural sewage treatment capability."
      ],
      "id": "9q8ufno"
